.TH YTNEFPRINT 1 "" "ytnef" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ytnefprint \- print the contents of TNEF (winmail.dat) streams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ytnefprint
.RI [ options ] " file" ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ytnefprint
parses Microsoft TNEF streams, the
.I application/ms-tnef
attachments usually named
.IR winmail.dat ,
and prints their message fields, attachments and MAPI properties.
It never writes files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose output. Repeat for more detail.
.TP
.BI \-s " n"
Set the largest attachment size to accept, in megabytes.
.TP
.B \-h
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ytnef (1)
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/Yeraze/ytnef
